WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.156
The I O tab connects the synth to the outside world.

2
00:00:04.156 --> 00:00:04.953
First, MIDI.

3
00:00:04.953 --> 00:00:07.944
Click Connect MIDI, and pick your controller.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.833
To map a knob, choose a target, click Learn, then move the control.

5
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:13.694
Here, Z Push.

6
00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.406
Now the controller plays the depth directly.

7
00:00:16.406 --> 00:00:18.512
Each binding has its own curve and range.

8
00:00:19.626 --> 00:00:23.534
MIDI clock in sets the tempo from a drum machine or a DAW.

9
00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.893
The readout shows the incoming BPM.

10
00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:28.588
Clock Out sends the tempo the other way.

11
00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:35.899
OSC works over the network, from TouchOSC, Max, or SuperCollider, through the small bridge in the tools folder.

12
00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:38.186
Enter the bridge address and connect.

13
00:00:38.639 --> 00:00:43.375
Learn works the same way: choose H Size, click Learn, and send a message.

14
00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:47.554
Every OSC message on that address now moves the parameter.

15
00:00:47.554 --> 00:00:51.403
Copy TouchOSC layout gives you a ready-made control surface.

16
00:00:51.856 --> 00:00:57.862
MIDI and OSC sources also exist as graph nodes, for patching instead of mapping.

17
00:00:57.862 --> 00:01:00.865
Next: control voltage, gamepads and MCP.
